---
/**
 * Terms of Use.
 *
 * Scoped to what this website actually is: a set of informational pages with
 * one contact form that opens the reader's own mail application. The previous
 * WordPress terms carried clauses for account registration and user-submitted
 * content, neither of which has ever existed on the Astro site; those are gone
 * rather than reworded.
 *
 * The governing-law and severability positions are carried over from the
 * previous document, which stated Indonesian law and Indonesian courts. They
 * are marked for confirmation rather than assumed to still be the intent.
 */
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import PageHero from "../components/sections/PageHero.jsx";

const EFFECTIVE = "[TO BE CONFIRMED — publication date]";
---

<BaseLayout
  metaKey="terms-of-use.html"
  title="Terms of Use"
  description="Terms for using the Immersia website: how our published material may be used, what our service pages do and do not commit us to, external links, and limitation of liability."
>
  <PageHero label="Legal" title="Terms of Use" />

  <article class="articlebody">
    <p class="lead">
      These terms cover your use of the Immersia website. They are short because
      the site is simple: pages to read, publications to reference, and one form
      that opens an email in your own mail application.
    </p>

    <div class="prose">
      <p>Effective {EFFECTIVE}. By using this website you accept these terms.</p>

      <h2>What this website is</h2>
      <p>
        This website publishes information about Immersia and our work:
        descriptions of our services, records of past engagements,
        representative publications, and written material on impact practice.
        It is a reference, not a service you sign into. There are no accounts,
        no subscriptions, and nothing to buy here.
      </p>

      <h2>Informational content</h2>
      <p>
        Our articles, publications, and service descriptions are general
        professional material. They describe methods and approaches; they are
        not advice for any specific organization, program, or decision. Applying
        a method described here to your own situation requires judgment about
        that situation, which a web page cannot supply.
      </p>
      <p>
        We aim to keep what we publish accurate and current, but we do not
        warrant that every page is complete or up to date. Some pages describe
        work completed in earlier years and are kept as a record.
      </p>

      <h2>Service descriptions are not offers</h2>
      <p>
        The service pages describe what we do. They are not an offer capable of
        acceptance and do not commit us to any scope, timeline, or fee. Work
        between Immersia and a client is governed by a separate written
        agreement, and only by that agreement.
      </p>
      <p>
        Sending a proposal request does not create a client relationship, and
        neither does our reply to it.
      </p>

      <h2>Intellectual property</h2>
      <p>
        The text, images, publications, structure, and design of this website
        belong to Immersia or to those who licensed them to us. Client and
        partner names and marks appearing on this site belong to their
        respective owners.
      </p>
      <p>
        You may read, quote, and cite our published material with attribution to
        Immersia and, where practical, a link to the page you took it from.
        Reproducing substantial parts of it, republishing it, or using it in a
        commercial product requires our written permission. Write to
        <a href="mailto:info@immersia.id">info@immersia.id</a> to ask.
      </p>
      <p>
        The reports behind our publication summaries contain client and program
        information that is not public, and are not distributed through this
        site.
      </p>

      <h2>Acceptable use</h2>
      <p>
        Use this website lawfully. Do not attempt to disrupt it, gain
        unauthorized access to it or to the systems that serve it, or use
        automated means to place a burden on it that a normal reader would not.
      </p>

      <h2>External links</h2>
      <p>
        This site links to WhatsApp, Instagram, and LinkedIn. Those services are
        operated by other companies. We do not control them and are not
        responsible for their content, availability, or practices. Following a
        link takes you outside this website and outside these terms.
      </p>

      <h2>Limitation of liability</h2>
      <p>
        This website is provided as it is. To the extent permitted by applicable
        law, Immersia is not liable for loss or damage arising from the use of
        this website or from reliance on its general informational content,
        including loss of profit, loss of data, or consequential loss.
      </p>
      <p>
        Nothing in these terms limits liability that cannot be limited by law.
      </p>
      <p>
        This limitation concerns the website. Liability under a signed
        engagement with Immersia is governed by that engagement.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes to these terms</h2>
      <p>
        We may update these terms as the website changes. The current version is
        the one published on this page, with its effective date shown above.
      </p>

      <h2>Governing law</h2>
      <p>
        These terms are governed by the laws of Indonesia, and disputes arising
        from them fall to the competent courts of Indonesia.
        <strong>[TO BE CONFIRMED — carried over from the previous website;
        confirm on legal review.]</strong>
      </p>
      <p>
        If any provision of these terms is found unenforceable, the remaining
        provisions continue to apply.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Immersia, Jl. Sepat No.43, Kebagusan, Ps. Minggu, Jakarta Selatan 12520,
        Indonesia. Email <a href="mailto:info@immersia.id">info@immersia.id</a>.
      </p>
      <p>
        See also our <a href="/privacy-policy.html">Privacy Policy</a> and
        <a href="/disclaimer.html">Disclaimer</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
